<title>UK: Eurotunnel promises dividend outlook.</title>
<headline>Eurotunnel promises dividend outlook.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eurotunnel SA said on Thursday that it would comment on its dividend prospects when it publishes its prospectus for debt restructuring plan in May.</p>
<p>&quot;We will tell you when we present the prospectus in the second half of May,&quot; Patrick Ponsolle, co-chairman, told a news conference.  </p>
<p>Earlier the Anglo-French company reported it made a loss last year of 685 million stg, most of it because of interest payments due on its total debt of nearly nine billion stg.</p>
<p>But it said it narrowed its operating loss before interest to 33 million stg from 192 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>If the restructuring plan goes ahead, Ponsolle said that the company expected its fixed-interest bill to drop to around 400 million stg compared to interest due last year of 615 million.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
